"""Roadmap 293 NARROWED (Deli Counter 0.254.0: an exploded axonometric of every building, with architectural
cutaways). Copied from `patch_roadmap_292_npc_body.py`: replaces 293's status block (the paragraph directly above its
heading, asserted to be the one this was written against) with one that keeps it after "Earlier status kept:". The
index is NOT touched here: run `python tools/roadmap_status.py --write` then `--check` after it.

    python patches/patch_roadmap_293_axonometric.py && python tools/roadmap_status.py --write && python tools/roadmap_status.py --check
"""
import pathlib
import sys

ROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
RM = ROOT / "PIPELINE_ROADMAP.md"

ITEMS = [(293, '\n\n**293. The floorplan tool draws each storey flat, and nothing shows how a building\'s storeys stack: an exploded axonometric view with architectural cutaways.** The walker, 2026-10-21, filing the guide: "add this to the roadmap to make our floorplan tool better and acheive that Exploded axonometric view, with architectural cutaways". `deli_counter/floorplan.py` renders one SVG a storey -- rooms, walls, typed openings, stairs with their destinations, ladders, open-to-below, furniture, markers, a scale and a legend -- offline, with no Blender and no generative model, so a designer judges the space rather than a table. Nothing draws a building in three dimensions as a diagram: no axonometric, isometric, exploded or cutaway view exists in any of the ten tool repositories (read again), and the only 3D presentations are `tools/look_shots.gd`\'s perspective overview and straight-on orthographic elevations and `migrations/review_render.py`\'s Cycles perspective shots. The guide\'s section 6 is the view the walker means: roofs and selected ceilings hidden, walls cut away where they hide the interiors, each floor raised by a display offset and kept aligned with the rest, an angled orthographic camera, outlines, restrained shading, floor labels and callouts -- the offsets the drawing\'s alone, never the elevations, collision or navigation. A spec already states most of what it reads (`spec_types.py`: storey height, wall and floor thickness, roofs, openings with sill and height, stairwells with their storeys, slab holes, floor holes and hatches); a floor\'s elevation and a wall\'s height are derived in `deli_counter.py`; a ceiling height, an atrium through several storeys and a partition\'s own thickness are stated nowhere. The plan disagrees with what is built in two places a 3D view would inherit (read again): partitions drawn 0.15 m thick and built at `wall_thick` (`floorplan.py:37` against `deli_counter.py:1750-1757`), and the storey height labelled "clg" (`floorplan.py:604-605`) where it is floor to floor. It leaves out ramps, platforms, fire escapes, parapets, roofs and ceilings. Plans are made only by `validate.py`, which the commit gate runs, into the ignored `build/floorplans/` (2,052 SVGs, half of them sightline overlays); `build.py --all`, and so a cold run, makes none, and Level Factory\'s `packages/service/facade.py:350-352` looks for a `lot_out/floorplan.svg` that nothing writes. **What would close it:** an exploded axonometric of every building, drawn from its spec beside its plans and offline and deterministic like them -- each storey\'s slab at its true elevation plus a display offset, walls standing to a cutaway height so the rooms read from above, openings as gaps, stairs and ladders drawn between the storeys they join, slab holes and floor holes as voids, roofs and ceilings left off, markers riding their storey\'s offset, room labels and a storey key -- with the offset applied to the drawing alone; the plan\'s two disagreements fixed first, and ramps, platforms and fire escapes drawn where they stand; the guide\'s acceptance checks (its section 10) asked of a test building -- a doorway moved or widened, a stair moved, an atrium\'s opening kept, two markers one above the other, the floors separated with their markers, the elevations unchanged -- and of a library building in a frame for the walker; made where the plans are made, and shown where a reviewer looks (a walker-review page, a level\'s export), chosen with the walker.', "*STATUS: OPEN 2026-10-21 -- the walker's floor-plan guide (`docs/reference/Floor_Plan_to_3D_Layout_and_Automap_Guide.md`), chased in `docs/findings/guides_2026-10-21/floor_plan.md`; not started.*", "*STATUS: NARROWED 2026-10-21 -- the exploded axonometric drawn, for every building. Deli Counter 0.254.0 (00c50db9, `patches/patch_dc_axonometric.py`): `axonometric.py` draws every storey at once from its spec, seen from above and to the south-west at true-isometric elevation -- each slab raised by a display offset that never moves an elevation (a storey's `data-elevation` beside its `data-offset`; the gap derived as the least rise that keeps one slab's drawing clear of the next, plus 2 m), walls standing to the 1.2 m plan cut with dark cut faces, doors as gaps with their thresholds, a window's sill wall and glass under the cut, furniture to the cut, roofs and ceilings off, every slab hole masked open with the slab's thickness on its far edges, stairs joined to the storey they climb to by an ascent line and alignment columns, ladders and open-to-below drop lines, markers on their storey, labels and a legend; offline and deterministic, the whole library in under a second, and `validate.py` writes `<name>.axo.svg` beside the plans, so the commit gate draws every building's. One layout, two drawings: the plan's wall arithmetic is `floorplan.wall_split` and `storey_walls`, refactored first with all 288 plans of the 159 specs byte for byte as before; the plan's two disagreements fixed -- a partition drawn at its built thickness (242 plans move, exactly those with a partition) and the storey height called floor to floor -- and `build_freshness.py` files both drawings as readers, so a change to one no longer reads every shell as stale. The guide's acceptance checks asked of library buildings in `test_axonometric.py` (8): the offset the drawing's alone, a doorway moved moving its gap in both drawings, a stair moved moving its flight and column, an atrium kept open, two markers one above the other on their own floors, every library building drawing every storey; frames of deli_a03, office and cbp_town_finale shown to the walker (`patches/dc_axonometric/axo_*.png`). No cold run: a build makes no drawing and the shells did not move. LEFT: ramps, platforms and fire escapes in either drawing; stairs drawn as treads rather than an ascent line; where a reviewer finds the drawing beside a level (a walker-review page, a level's export), chosen with the walker; the guide's section 8 for this view -- floors selected and the rest subdued -- belongs with roadmap 295's map. Earlier status kept: OPEN 2026-10-21 -- the walker's floor-plan guide (`docs/reference/Floor_Plan_to_3D_Layout_and_Automap_Guide.md`), chased in `docs/findings/guides_2026-10-21/floor_plan.md`; not started.*")]


def main():
    raw = RM.read_bytes()
    if b"\r\n" in raw:
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: the roadmap is LF and CRLF was found; nothing written")
    text = raw.decode("utf-8")
    for n, heading, old, new in ITEMS:
        if new[:80] in text:
            raise SystemExit("REFUSED: %d already applied; nothing written" % n)
        if text.count(heading) != 1:
            raise SystemExit("REFUSED: %d's heading is not there once; nothing written" % n)
        h = text.find(heading)
        s = text.rindex("\n\n", 0, h) + 2
        if text[s:h] != old:
            raise SystemExit("REFUSED: %d's status block is not the one this was written against; nothing written" % n)
        text = text[:s] + new + text[h:]
        if text.count(new + heading) != 1:
            raise SystemExit("REFUSED: %d's status no longer adjoins its heading; nothing written" % n)
    RM.write_bytes(text.encode("utf-8"))
    print("roadmap 293: NARROWED, the earlier status kept; now roadmap_status.py --write / --check")
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
